{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting","id":828343,"title":"How to make the Circle interesting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-11T12:11:58-08:00","id":828343,"title":"How to make the Circle interesting?","content":"So the Circle of the Crone. They seem to have a lot of aesthetic appeal to players. Pagans are cool, pagan vampires are cool, cults are cool and bloody blood magic is cool. But increasingly, I've been frustrated by them in setting building and trying to understand them. I really dig the aesthetic appeal, but sometimes I worry that I'm only seeing the style and not the substance.<br /> <br /> To give context, I think the Sanctified have this substance in spades. What they represent, the shift in mentality from living to dead and the accompanying theological assumption that change carry a lot of appeal to me. That they provide a strong sense of purpose for Kindred, a code of behavior and a doctrine of complex beliefs that can be debated is really intriguing.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm trying to find the same meat in the Circle of the Crone. What do they do? What things can actually divide them? What heady content can characters engage with in the Circle of the Crone?<br /> <br /> Just to make it clear, I like them, I'm just frustrated because I feel like I just don't get as much from them as I do from the Sanctified. I think I'm going to be playing a potential member of the Circle of the Crone in an upcoming game so some ideas to work with would definitely be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:07:18-08:00","id":828373,"title":"","content":"I think the Crone are a mirror to the Sanctified in a lot of ways. They also represent a shift in mentality from living to dead and carry theological assumptions that go along with that change. They even both teach their adherents to embrace the monster they have become. The key difference is that the Sanctified view it as a curse or an obligation, where the Circle view it as a blessing or a privilege.<br /> <br /> For me, the Circle of the Crone is to the Lancea et Sanctum as the Carthian Movement is to the Invictus. Like the Carthians, they are united when they are oppressed (or percieve themselves to be) and divided when they are in power. United in public, divided behind closed doors. The issues that divide them are spiritual rather than political, but the same generalities apply. Which Gods should be revered? What is the right way to appease them? Who should or shouldn't be allowed to participate in their veneration and in what capacity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-11-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:31:43-08:00","id":828397,"title":"","content":"Also of note, I think, is the question of &quot;What is/are god(s)&quot; and what does Cruac have to do with this? Some might believe that Cruac is a perversion of the gods because it leashes them and steals their power, while others might believe that Cruac <i><b>is</b></i> the power of the gods given to them through blood. Some would say that gods should be revered, others would say they should be feared, others would say they should be leashed.<br /> <br /> What of the Draugrs? They're monsters, so why should we fear them rather than embrace our monstrosity like they did? Should we Ghoul a little army or should we keep the power of the blood? Should we unite and fight as one or fight amongst ourselves to create a single powerful being with his lone acolyte, Sith-like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:31:56-08:00","id":828400,"title":"","content":"Being one of the Kindred is fucking horrible unless you were a particularly unpleasant sort of person in life. The Circle are the ones who can most easily help a freshly Embraced individual come to terms with things - not by playing at the worst parts of human society, not by becoming a zealot who feels forsaken by God, and certainly not by subjecting yourself to occult experiments, but just by doing what comes naturally.<br /> <br /> Don't worry about all this. These urges are natural and perfectly fine; healthy, even! No need to feel bad, because this is what you are now. Doesn't feeding feel good? Isn't it empowering to do the things you never could've dreamed of before, to no longer be one of the sheep? <br /> <br /> Before anything of doctrine and faith, the Circle is about acceptance of monstrosity. That has to be a comforting option for many new vampires, who likely feel somewhere between addicts and sex offenders due to their new unholy condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-21-2016, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:20:13-08:00","id":828464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=828400#post828400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being one of the Kindred is fucking horrible unless you were a particularly unpleasant sort of person in life. The Circle are the ones who can most easily help a freshly Embraced individual come to terms with things - not by playing at the worst parts of human society, not by becoming a zealot who feels forsaken by God, and certainly not by subjecting yourself to occult experiments, but just by doing what comes naturally.<br /> <br /> Don't worry about all this. These urges are natural and perfectly fine; healthy, even! No need to feel bad, because this is what you are now. Doesn't feeding feel good? Isn't it empowering to do the things you never could've dreamed of before, to no longer be one of the sheep?<br /> <br /> Before anynof the do trine and faith, the Circle is about <b>acceptance of monstrosity</b>. That has to be a comforting option for many new vampires, who likely feel somewhere between addicts and sex offenders due to their new unholy condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realized I'd forgotten the bolded, which is a cool thing to keep in mind. I guess the other thing I'm wondering about is what they do beyond reveling in their monstrousness. The Sanctified protect the flock and punish those who stray/threaten them. They keep histories of the Kindred as well as Relics. I'm trying to figure out what the Circle gets up to on a night-by-night basis too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:58:45-08:00","id":828481,"title":"","content":"I had the circle as antagonists in a werewolf game I ran recently. <br /> <br /> They were very much involved with Ghost, Spirits, and Angels. The top coterie of the cult was actually rescued by a powerful spirit from a Strix, so they began to worship it and do its bidding. <br /> <br /> They mainly did two things. The first is that they ran mystery cults. The mortal cultists were sacraficing their blood to be transformed into something higher in exchange for the guidance and leadership of the Ghouls and Kindred who controlled these cults. Mostly it was motivational speaking with a few select members being selected for feeding at the end of them. They played the various roles of ancient pagan priests would in society for good or for worse in exchange for blood. <br /> <br /> The next thing they did was attempt to make sacrifices to their Spirit and Ghost allies who could help them control the city and prevent the Strix from destroying them. There are a few 1E disciplines that really help with this along with Blood Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T16:40:52-08:00","id":828495,"title":"","content":"What exactly keeps the Circle from having those concerns? Mind, for some covens they aren't a flock: they're cattle.<br /> <br /> The Circle trucks with their gods. They deal with the hungry shadows, their faith to them isn't blind, because most often than not, they can deal with the object of their veneration, like you can with people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T17:01:49-08:00","id":828502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=828464#post828464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realized I'd forgotten the bolded, which is a cool thing to keep in mind. I guess the other thing I'm wondering about is what they do beyond reveling in their monstrousness. The Sanctified protect the flock and punish those who stray/threaten them. They keep histories of the Kindred as well as Relics. I'm trying to figure out what the Circle gets up to on a night-by-night basis too.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've got heathen blood Gods to appease. That can take a lot of work, depending on how demanding their Gods are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:13:19-08:00","id":828546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=828464#post828464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realized I'd forgotten the bolded, which is a cool thing to keep in mind. I guess the other thing I'm wondering about is what they do beyond reveling in their monstrousness. The Sanctified protect the flock and punish those who stray/threaten them. They keep histories of the Kindred as well as Relics. I'm trying to figure out what the Circle gets up to on a night-by-night basis too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also recall that they are heavily invested in acts of creation. So they probably spend a good amount of time doing stuff like painting or manipulating mortals in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T04:26:16-08:00","id":828720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=828373#post828373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the Circle of the Crone is to the Lancea et Sanctum as the Carthian Movement is to the Invictus. Like the Carthians, they are united when they are oppressed (or percieve themselves to be) and divided when they are in power. United in public, divided behind closed doors. The issues that divide them are spiritual rather than political, but the same generalities apply. Which Gods should be revered? What is the right way to appease them? Who should or shouldn't be allowed to participate in their veneration and in what capacity?</div> </div> </div> </div> Dear gods this. Last time I played a Crone game set in the South, I was a voodoo themed Acolyte, and the rest of the CotC was fairly strongly stereotypical vampire-Wicca, like described in the Covenant book. I actually got chewed out for not taking one of the Maid/Mother/Crone/Scarlet figures as inspiration. It got to the point where she all but shunned her covenant mates for being self righteous, dogmatic zealots. Yes, the CotC in this city were the ones who were obsessed with blind faith and heresies. <br /> <br /> And, you know? That's completely in theme for them. In a lot of ways, the CotC is like a reaction or counterculture against the predominance of Abrahamic religions. They're only united because 1) Cruac and 2) rejection of the patriarchal LeS. That second point has a lot of real world analogs - while there are plenty of reactions against racist/sexist/anti-LGBT/antisemitic faiths, and they tend to lock step against an oppressive force, none of them really agree on anything besides the oppressive force needs to back down. The CotC has it good compared to the real world, because at least they have Cruac as another point of union. Even then? Look at the Cruac Style merits. Some focus on primal nature and life itself. Some on shadows and darkness. And some on Chaos and mutations. And there are likely others as well.<br /> <br /> So, what is the Circle? They're a collection of non-Abrahamic faiths and cults. They, unlike most other covenants, are highly diverse. You can have any faith you want, and you'll generally be part of the Circle. And, usually, most Circles are more than tolerant of it. In fact, they champion that freedom. Its all about the personal faith with them. About following your own path alongside your fellows. The CotC also tends to have a bit of a Gangrel mindset to it. What does that mean? Each cult tends to think and operate a lot like a pack. Working in unison like a family against the world, both physically and magically. <br /> <br /> These individual cults form the core of the CotC. I tend to see each cult as separate cotories that happen to work together because they share a few goals. So, if you want the substance of the Circle, you focus on these individual cults, giving snapshots of each, how they compare and contrast, and still work together against the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=828464#post828464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realized I'd forgotten the bolded, which is a cool thing to keep in mind. I guess the other thing I'm wondering about is what they do beyond reveling in their monstrousness. The Sanctified protect the flock and punish those who stray/threaten them. They keep histories of the Kindred as well as Relics. I'm trying to figure out what the Circle gets up to on a night-by-night basis too.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, reveling is a large part of the Circle. Most vampire covenants have a strong focus on order and structure. The Lance, the Invictus, the Ordo. Even the Carthians have a self policing structure through popular opinion, though they're much more lax than most. But the Circle? They're all about finding a kind of peace with the Beast and reveling in their existance. They hunt, they tend their mandrake gardens, they challenge themselves through adversary. Connect with the world. <br /> <br /> Part of the whole point of the Circle is that there isn't some grand design. They're the <i>rejection </i>of such structure. They're anarchy*. And what they tend to do on a nightly basis is make sure that there's no one who's going to tell them they can't do whatever they want. Many posters will be familiar with the rede, &quot;Do what you will but harm none.&quot; The Circle is very proactive in making sure that no force out there is going to telling them what to do. Even each other. because vampires are controlling assholes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Yes, I know that the write up suggests that the CotC is &quot;Less anarchy,and more the rule of the strong without formal laws or any pretense of \u201ccivilization.\u201d&quot; But that's really the whole end game of anarchy in the first place. And still a very Gangrel-y mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T06:22:32-08:00","id":828756,"title":"","content":"They're also pretty flexible on that &quot;harm none&quot; bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T07:28:29-08:00","id":828775,"title":"","content":"Oh, yes. Definitely. So focused on the first part I forgot about the second!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T08:49:17-08:00","id":828813,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of things can divide them, as stated before, they are a collection of pagan cults and the face they put on the Crone may diverge a lot from a sub pagan culture to another. For instance, in Chicago the Hierophant is Rowen and she has an Indian way to look at the Crone, not sure it's very appealing to neopagans or that it would ring any bell at all for more modern vampires. Not only the Crone can go by many names but she might have different attributes and/or philosophies. Sure, the core book describes the principles common to Accolytes but there is a lot of room for the specifics and the devil is in details. When the CotC is persecuted that can put these differences aside and unite but, when they are relatively accepted and numerous (like they are in Chicago) they would be divided: not the same myth of creation, not the same name for the Crone, not the same rituals.<br /> As for reveling in their monstrosity, yes that's what they claim but they can't just run wild and give the Beast its due, lest they'll turn into Draugr at an alarming speed. I tend to think, they consider a vampire is part Man part Beast and they try to reach a balance, teaching the Man coaching the Beast, til they reach a kind of equilibrium. Totally different from the Brood that ultimately aim at stripping themselves of every ounce of humanity. That being said, how do you reach this equilibrium ? What is part of your vampiric nature (besides the obvious), which behavior is about understanding your true self and which is just indulgence and losing it to the Beast ?<br /> <br /> I think, there's more meat to this covenant than first meet the eyes, than sheer style and flavor (and I love that too) and you might even make a city totally controlled by the Circle with many feuds and religious rivalries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:35:43-08:00","id":828831,"title":"","content":"There's a city ruled by the Circle in the Gangrel clanbook, it seemed really cool.<br /> <br /> My favorite covenant of the main five, but everyone seems to have answered already.<br /> <br /> I think the additions to Cruac in the upcoming Secrets of the Covenants will help a lot, and obviously the Circle chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T13:43:08-08:00","id":828940,"title":"","content":"This kinda reminds me of a game where the Circle awoken a Native American Elder with the mistaken idea that they would give their blessing to the cult.<br /> <br /> The result was a metaphorical and quite literal culling of classical european romantic paganism and being replaced with a cult that is more authentic to the region.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, it still worked out in the style of the Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:56:49-08:00","id":828995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=828940#post828940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kinda reminds me of a game where the Circle awoken a Native American Elder with the mistaken idea that they would give their blessing to the cult.<br /> <br /> The result was a metaphorical and quite literal culling of classical european romantic paganism and being replaced with a cult that is more authentic to the region.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, it still worked out in the style of the Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope we can one day get an official treatment of a Native American covenant, or what their influence on a standard domain might look like. I think someone on the old forums did one once?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T20:47:46-08:00","id":829094,"title":"","content":"It is a very big blind spot that is worth visiting. Really, the only issue that I see is too much borrowing from Werewolf's themes but that shouldn't be that much of an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T21:25:41-08:00","id":829104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=829094#post829094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a very big blind spot that is worth visiting. Really, the only issue that I see is too much borrowing from Werewolf's themes but that shouldn't be that much of an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf doesn't have much to do with Native American culture or folklore at all other than some ties to animism/shamanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:19:53-08:00","id":830002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting#post828343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Circle of the Crone. They seem to have a lot of aesthetic appeal to players. Pagans are cool, pagan vampires are cool, cults are cool and bloody blood magic is cool. But increasingly, I've been frustrated by them in setting building and trying to understand them. I really dig the aesthetic appeal, but sometimes I worry that I'm only seeing the style and not the substance.<br /> <br /> To give context, I think the Sanctified have this substance in spades. What they represent, the shift in mentality from living to dead and the accompanying theological assumption that change carry a lot of appeal to me. That they provide a strong sense of purpose for Kindred, a code of behavior and a doctrine of complex beliefs that can be debated is really intriguing.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm trying to find the same meat in the Circle of the Crone. What do they do? What things can actually divide them? What heady content can characters engage with in the Circle of the Crone?<br /> <br /> Just to make it clear, I like them, I'm just frustrated because I feel like I just don't get as much from them as I do from the Sanctified. I think I'm going to be playing a potential member of the Circle of the Crone in an upcoming game so some ideas to work with would definitely be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an elder in my version of the circle stated, &quot;We are spiritual path not a religion. Religion is for those afraid of going to hell.Spirituality is for those who have been to hell and back. Once you understand that you understand the nature of the conflict between us and the Lance.&quot;<br /> <br /> My version of the circle doesn't prosletyze. But it does accept seekers as students it sees as worthy. I argue that they are based on historic mystery cults as such outsiders are not aware of the internal structure. It adds to their mystique and is a defense mechanism(hard to target the leaders) . And it keeps the other Covenants guessing as well.<br /> <br /> They can anyone of the factions from old book. They could be Strigoi. Backwoods hoodoo artists. The entire folk magic spectrum is open for interpretation. Or at least the cthonic or darker ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T19:27:28-08:00","id":831427,"title":"","content":"It's worth pointing out that the Circle's style comes from a very specific type of paganism. A North/Western style, mainly Celtic, if you want a more structured religion to form the base look at ancient Roman paganism. A very hierarchical, structured religion. You could even use the fact that many pagans were fractious as well and had wildly different cultures and viewpoints. Ancient roman and Greek cultures were very patriarchal and their religions reflected this. Maybe a Roman pagan chafes under this wild neopagan nonsense but allies with them against the Spear. Or perhaps bring variant pagan beliefs in conflict with the basic tenants of the circle. Egyptian God worshiping pagans would likely find the Celtic inspired Circle distasteful to say the least.<br /> <br /> You could point out the difference in neopaganism compared to classical paganism. Wicca may have the harm none rule but ancient celts certainly didn't and were very warlike. Ancient Druids might have even been into human sacrificing. The circle might be divided along age lines because of those radical shifts in thinking. Elder Circle members may scoff at young neopagan vampires and seek to turn them into proper blood drenched monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3581-salubri87","name":"Salubri87","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:56:12-08:00","id":831837,"title":"","content":"Considering their semi-fluid beliefs and preoccupation with pagan gods/spirits, it's not unheard of for them to actually trap, contact, or draw the attention of any of the CoD's ephemeral entities, <i>wildly </i>misinterpret how it happened, what it is, and/or what it wants, and ascribe it religious significance and a Covenant role. <br /> <br /> Willingly doing the bidding of a hypothetical Monstrous Mother is hard enough; unknowingly doing the bidding of an actual spirit of painful bloodletting masquerading as a &quot;sainted&quot; Lady Xoc is an entirely new set of complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:25:54-08:00","id":831904,"title":"","content":"Scrap the wildly misinterpret part and you more or less still have it right.<br /> <br /> Though that may be just my preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:03:20-08:00","id":831944,"title":"","content":"I have to agree. I don't think making them out to be stooges and ignorant is going to make them more interesting to people who see a problem with them to begin with.<br /> <br /> A big step a person might make in making them more interesting would be to flesh out the Crone. Some people find the amorphousness of the Circle to be too troubling, and they don't seem to be getting past the idea that things like spirits can be gods and not, 'just a spirit.' So make the Crone out to be some ancient vampiric progenitor who speaks to them through their blood and their Beast. The Danse Macabre has a 'gonzo' covenant, the Mother's Army, which was at least partially combined with the Circle in second edition. The Mother's Army is a far more militant bent to the concept, with a sort of 'you will be assimilated' mindset, but it's easy to pare down to something more playable, and even keep that aggressive mindset for certain factions within it.<br /> <br /> They have three primary goals. 'Get everyone on board,' with everyone supping from Mother's Vitae, which lets her speak to you. Again that can be taken down a notch or played up for the more zealous, forcing the Vitae down their throats. ' Awaken her children,' which gives you a lot of eldritch horrors and ways to incorporate the various Other Things into the game. And 'learn all the mother's secrets,' which is a good reason to embrace the magic, because it was in you all along and Mother just wants you to be the best you can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:38:08-08:00","id":831982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=831904#post831904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scrap the wildly misinterpret part and you more or less still have it right.<br /> <br /> Though that may be just my preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think I'd like to have them be unknowing about that sort of thing. I think deliberately mythologizing these potential figures, fully knowing that it's part of the story is sort of interesting. It reminds me of how a lot of my studies of people in antiquity have sold a more complicated view of their religion than simply believing that Zeus or Jupiter are literally responsible for the lightning in the sky and other such things. Given the Circle's ancestors and sources it makes good sense that they'd do so, but it also seems like an essential quality of syncretism is the understanding that people have agency in shaping their beliefs. I think part of the problem with assuming them to be dupes is projecting our obsession with literal truth onto their beliefs, when literal truth is often irrelevant (deliberately so) to the beliefs and practices of many groups of people.<br /> <br /> The truth of whether the Spirit is actually a goddess is way less important than the role that Goddess serves for the cult. If she fills them with the ecstatic bloodlust that they desire and facilitates their ritual acceptance of the Beast, it <i>doesn't matter</i>. Perhaps that's another thing about the Circle that makes them scary. The truth is not a weapon you can use against them, they're not ignorant stooges who will falter when you prove their Goddess didn't make the world in seven days. They'll get the last laugh when she's worked them up into the frenzy that rips your throat out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T13:54:14-08:00","id":832041,"title":"","content":"I've always thought with 2e that the Circle Of The Crone had great potential and very evocative, flexible spirituality (even though my favorite covenant is the Lancea Et Sanctum), but I could never quite form a concrete picture of how that looked and I always felt like I was missing something that actually struck the core of it. In that, this thread has been very enlightening, particularly the latest exchanges. It's finally clicked for me that I was funnily enough trying to look too critically at the beliefs and figures any branch of the Circle would actually congregate around or pursue.<br /> <br /> Their idols and deities, invented or found, are important because of what they represent, and not what they actually are or how someone else empirically classifies them. Their message and beliefs are important in and of themselves, and not because of the mythos chosen to focus them, the explanation that gives them a place in an existing perspective, or the methods by which they're spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-17-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T06:30:01-08:00","id":832474,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Leetsepeak;n831982]<br /> <br /> Yeah, I don't think I'd like to have them be unknowing about that sort of thing. I think deliberately mythologizing these potential figures, fully knowing that it's part of the story is sort of interesting. It reminds me of how a lot of my studies of people in antiquity have sold a more complicated view of their religion than simply believing that Zeus or Jupiter are literally responsible for the lightning in the sky and other such things. Given the Circle's ancestors and sources it makes good sense that they'd do so, but it also seems like an essential quality of syncretism is the understanding that people have agency in shaping their beliefs. I think part of the problem with assuming them to be dupes is projecting our obsession with literal truth onto their beliefs, when literal truth is often irrelevant (deliberately so) to the beliefs and practices of many groups of people.<br /> <br /> The truth of whether the Spirit is actually a goddess is way less important than the role that Goddess serves for the cult. If she fills them with the ecstatic bloodlust that they desire and facilitates their ritual acceptance of the Beast, it <i>doesn't matter</i>. Perhaps that's another thing about the Circle that makes them scary. The truth is not a weapon you can use against them, they're not ignorant stooges who will falter when you prove their Goddess didn't make the world in seven days. They'll get the last laugh when she's worked them up into the frenzy that rips your throat out.[/QUOTE<br /> <br /> I need to look at the spirits cruac (and Spirits) again and look at how spirits as gods would work. <br /> Spirits of blood and hungers need to be looked at. In my case my Nos elder was a family traditionalist pagan in Brittany.<br /> I see him, as a Haunt, translating the Dark Mother to the Morrigan A lady of Terror , Phantoms and the Mists.<br /> I'm sure there are few spirits who take one that roll or pass as her servants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T10:23:10-08:00","id":832580,"title":"","content":"*glances upthread in growing confusion*<br /> <br /> To be clear, my point was more that given their Animism-heavy philosophy, the Circle has both more inclination/opportunity to deal with actual spirits, and to do so with a more holistic, reverential approach than most. Since the Shadow isn't exactly vampires' wheelhouse, opportunistic spirits <i>can potentially</i> take advantage of the situation if they're inclined, from shrugging and accepting free essence, to manipulating their new mortal-ish acquaintances' beliefs.<br /> <br /> Or IOW, sometime actual interaction with actual spirits, not necessarily on the vampire's terms. <br /> <br /> I'm genuinely perplexed about how that got retreaded as &quot;Credulous Primitives Worship Anything, Wrongly&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 02-18-2016, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T10:49:57-08:00","id":832590,"title":"","content":"Well, it WAS animism heavy in 1e. And, yes, they tended to be mixed up with naughty, tricksy spirits that fooled them. In 2e, this really isn't the case anymore - no vampire covenant deals with animism by default. We deal in vampire-specific entities and magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T11:18:01-08:00","id":832618,"title":"","content":"I think people bristle at the idea of presenting any of the covenants as dupes by default because it makes them less legitimate in the eyes of others. While I didn't take what you said as being the norm, I do think it's worth emphasizing that I don't think spirits actually CAN take advantage of their beliefs because syncretic belief systems and the philosophy of the Circle of the Crone fundamentally don't seem to lend themselves to that kind of relationship.<br /> <br /> If there's an entity that they &quot;worship&quot; it strikes me that it should be a relationship of mutual use. The Circle uses the entity for the function it provides and the entity uses them by the exchange of what they'll do for it. Presenting them as the lesser in that power relationship by default on the basis of some weird notion of religious truth feels like something the Sanctified might do but not something reflective of the Circle's perspective on such a relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:31:21-08:00","id":834963,"title":"","content":"I think it is a great error to explicitly &quot;explain&quot; the Circle of the Crone. They are very much supposed to be... well, it feels cheap saying &quot;mysterious&quot;, but somewhat &quot;different&quot; could fit. If you need to start explaining them, do so in ways that are mutually inconsistent, or depend on wildly opposing sources of myths. And never have an acolyte explain exactly in which manner something worked. Give your players some causes, some effects, and let them squirm and shift uncomfortably with connecting the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T08:20:48-08:00","id":836417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/828343-how-to-make-the-circle-interesting?p=834963#post834963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is a great error to explicitly &quot;explain&quot; the Circle of the Crone. They are very much supposed to be... well, it feels cheap saying &quot;mysterious&quot;, but somewhat &quot;different&quot; could fit. If you need to start explaining them, do so in ways that are mutually inconsistent, or depend on wildly opposing sources of myths. And never have an acolyte explain exactly in which manner something worked. Give your players some causes, some effects, and let them squirm and shift uncomfortably with connecting the two.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I agree the players usually don't have cultural reference point on how mystery cults work.<br /> That is the biggest thing about people not getting the circle is they have nothing but certain tropes to connect it with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}